silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_03_quality_leg_concrete_anchor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "QualityLegConcreteAnchorExample" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_03_quality_leg_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'QualityLegConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, BodyMassQuality: the quality attribute of having a body mass; a BFO/PATO quality type (PATO:0000128) that inheres in Mittens; distinct from the numeric value 3450 and the measurement event WeightMeas_3450g; also, QualityArrow_BodyMass: the typed arrow BodyMassQuality -> MittensColimitApex; distinct from measurement_leg (WeightMeas_3450g -> MittensColimitApex); also, PATO_0000128: the Phenotype And Trait Ontology (PATO) term for mass quality; the ontological authority that classifies BodyMassQuality as a mass-type quality attribute." .
